1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,660
(knocks)

2
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:03,080
(Sheldon:)Come in.

3
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:06,870
(cats meowing)

4
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:09,070
(Amy:)Surprise.

5
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:11,870
(Sheldon:)Mom, what an unexpected pleasure.

6
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,710
(Mrs Cooper:)My, my, that's a powerful smell.

7
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:19,720
(Sheldon:)I'd like you to meet Oppenheimer,
Frisch, Panofsky,

8
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,430
(Sheldon:)Feynman, Weisskopf...

9
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:22,600
(Mrs Cooper:)Yeah, I get it.

10
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,390
(Mrs Cooper:)You got a lot of cats

11
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:26,410
(Mrs Cooper:)and you gave 'em cute Jewish names.

12
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:28,270
(Sheldon:)What are you doing here?

13
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:29,530
(Mrs Cooper:)Leonard called.

14
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:32,760
(Mrs Cooper:)And he said that you were
pining for a young lady.

15
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,560
(Sheldon:)Oh, that's preposterous.

16
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:36,600
(Sheldon:)I'm not pining over anyone.

17
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,700
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, lambchop, we can
quibble what to call it,

18
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,270
(Mrs Cooper:)but I think we can
both agree it's creepy.

19
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:45,370
(Sheldon:)I do not agree.

20
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,730
(Sheldon:)Cats make wonderful companions.

21
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:52,000
(Sheldon:)They don't argue or question
my intellectual authority,

22
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,880
(Sheldon:)and this little guy here,

23
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:57,140
(Sheldon:)I think you'll find
to be quite zazzy.

24
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:03,020
(Mrs Cooper:)You should have called sooner.

